 "_doc": [
  "Per-program FP/SIMD spill budget (ratchet) for grouped native NEON tile programs (row tiles 2-4).",
  "Keys: compiler identity (CMake compiler id + major version, also derived from the compiler --version output) -> ISA envelope -> rows:family:policy:encoding:map:minimum.",
  "family 0=ASIMD 1=SDOT 2=SMMLA; policy 0=BackendNative 1=GPUAlignedExpert; encoding 0=NibbleLUT 1=ExpandedInt8 2=Q6KNativeDualScale 4=NibbleLUTSourceScale 5=IQ3SExpandedSourceScale; map 0=Centered 1=Unsigned 2=NonLinear.",
  "A spill is one load/store instruction moving FP/SIMD data through a stack address that is not a proven ABI save/restore of d8-d15. Structural failures are fatal and are never budgeted.",
  "Single-row (decode) programs are not listed: they must not spill at all.",
  "Nonzero values are pre-existing grouped-tile register pressure (equal to the pre-R1 base within a few instructions); idea 29 tracks reducing them and the C4 panel work touches the same tiles.",
